<title>FRANCE: S&amp;P confirms Saint-Gobain ratings.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P confirms Saint-Gobain ratings.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ratings agency Standard &amp; Poor's confirmed on Tuesday its AA- senior unsecured and A-1+ commercial paper ratings of Cie de Saint-Gobain.</p>
<p>The move follows the announcement of Saint-Gobain's acquisition of the remaining 42 percent of the capital of U.S. glass maker Ball Foster it did not own.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said the outlook on Saint-Gobain's long-term debt remained negative.  </p>
<p>Saint-Gobain is buying out Ball-Foster for $190 million.</p>
<p>As part of the announced transactions, Ball-Foster will also acquire the assets and some liabilities of Anchor Glass Container Corp for $365 million.</p>
<p>The ratings confirmations take into account the strengthening of Saint-Gobain's positions in the U.S. glass-packaging market, S&amp;P said.</p>
<p>But it said these transactions, together with its acquisition of Poliet in May 1996, substantially reduced Saint-Gobain's financial flexibility to undertake any further acquisitions.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
